#: ../../source/docs/common-ads-b-receiver.rst:8
#: c66af7dd1a4b4f9dbd74c2638741383a
msgid "This article describes how to attach and configure an ADS-B module so that your aircraft can be aware of, and/or transmit to, other aircraft and air-traffic control nearby. This also allows the pilot on the ground to be aware of nearby manned aircraft and optionally to allow the vehicle to automatically avoid them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ads-b-receiver.rst:13
#: 525f47369b5c4525b2b5317860caa8f6
msgid "ADS-B (aka `Automatic Dependent Surveillance Broadcast <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Automatic_dependent_surveillance_%E2%80%93_broadcast>`__) is an air traffic surveillance technology that enables aircraft to be accurately tracked by air traffic controllers and other pilots without the need for conventional radar."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ads-b-receiver.rst:18
#: e6eb9ddbe1d9488fa09197e2fbb73a29
msgid "The avoidance features are new features still under development and should be used with caution. It is highly recommended that the RCx_OPTION =38 (ADSB Avoidance En) feature be setup if ADSB avoidance is enabled to allow easy disabling while airborne, if so desired."
msgstr ""

