#: ../../source/docs/common-ads-b-receiver.rst:83
#: 41d62646ca4444f1912b2312fdec848a
msgid "ADSB-out configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ads-b-receiver.rst:87
#: 213435fbb6704cbd9e20dcb22dbdc9d4
msgid "Ensure you have the correct permissions to be using ADSB hardware that is capable of transmitting. You will be showing up on air-traffic controller airport radar!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ads-b-receiver.rst:89
#: a9fb906fa3b14d179f84cbc688841fed
msgid "The following parameters are used to configure ADS-B out:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ads-b-receiver.rst:91
#: ca477716926544dda02786e91c1230fb
msgid ":ref:`ADSB_ICAO_ID <ADSB_ICAO_ID>`: ICAO_ID unique vehicle identification number of this aircraft. This is a integer limited to 24bits. If set to 0 then one will be randomly generated. If set to -1 then static information is not sent, transceiver is assumed pre-programmed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ads-b-receiver.rst:92
#: 4ee94a6ca0004b36964c751b98a99131
msgid ":ref:`ADSB_EMIT_TYPE <ADSB_EMIT_TYPE>`: ADSB classification for the type of vehicle emitting the transponder signal. Default value is 14 (UAV)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ads-b-receiver.rst:93
#: aa7259af970b454abe33502d4e36f829
msgid ":ref:`ADSB_LEN_WIDTH <ADSB_LEN_WIDTH>`: Aircraft length and width dimension options in Length and Width in meters. In most cases, use a value of 1 for smallest size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ads-b-receiver.rst:94
#: d854febe05eb4d9ab8e496359c4f3279
msgid ":ref:`ADSB_OFFSET_LAT <ADSB_OFFSET_LAT>`: GPS antenna lateral offset. This describes the physical location offset from center of the GPS antenna on the aircraft."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ads-b-receiver.rst:95
#: cb7f264e646143bc98b99c091d131b9a
msgid ":ref:`ADSB_OFFSET_LON <ADSB_OFFSET_LON>`: GPS antenna longitudinal offset. This is usually set to 1, Applied By Sensor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ads-b-receiver.rst:96
#: b6228770b4754e569a340c0c48f357cc
msgid ":ref:`ADSB_RF_SELECT <ADSB_RF_SELECT>`: Transceiver RF selection for Rx enable and/or Tx enable. This only effects devices that can Tx and/or Rx. Rx-only devices override this to always be Rx-only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ads-b-receiver.rst:97
#: a6682715f1fd405a858291f4a46eb3bf
msgid ":ref:`ADSB_SQUAWK <ADSB_SQUAWK>`: Squawk/Transponder (Mode 3/A) code that is broadcasted to ATC that is usually assigned by your ATC for a given flight. In the USA/Canada the default squawk code is for VFR which is 1200. Most parts of Europe and Australia use 7000. If an invalid octal number is set then it will be reset to 1200."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ads-b-receiver.rst:98
#: ab416cdbcf1f48a7a5f5ca8f176d9c98
msgid ":ref:`ADSB_OPTIONS <ADSB_OPTIONS>`: Allows enabling certain device specific capabilities and to allow \"Squawking\" emergency codes on certain vehicle failsafes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ads-b-receiver.rst:100
#: 420e8438c6564af78c213b366d33f44e
msgid "In many cases the defaults are OK and you don't need to change any of these except :ref:`ADSB_RF_SELECT <ADSB_RF_SELECT>` which is needed to turn on the transmitter. The :ref:`ADSB_RF_SELECT<ADSB_RF_SELECT>` transmit bit is cleared on boot to ensure you're only trsnamitting when intentionally enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ads-b-receiver.rst:102
#: d5b022ee12724d2e9fb55bc9d659a06c
msgid "There are additional MAVLink messages for ADSB in uavionix.xml to allow a GCS to set all of these options. Namely, msg UAVIONIX_ADSB_OUT_CFG and UAVIONIX_ADSB_OUT_DYNAMIC where the _cfg is the only place where you can assign a custom callsign."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ads-b-receiver.rst:104
#: e7ba897f6e0c4e5fa06f81db99ddff22
msgid "Mission Planner's transponder tab will not send correct messages to Sagetech's XP series transponders. In order to change operating mode, Sagetech's Engineering GUI can be used to set the transponder to ALT mode to ensure transmission is working with the flight controller."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ads-b-receiver.rst:107
#: 4edf4a4ce30b4db9989e557a5b0f26ae
msgid "Enabling Manned Vehicle Avoidance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ads-b-receiver.rst:109
#: 0beac7a6fe534a5996f9f08e0ca9d6f7
msgid "ArduPilot includes a flight mode, AVOID_ADSB, that attempts to avoid manned vehicles based on the ADS-B sensor's output. Entry into this mode is automatic when avoidance is necessary based on the parameters below. Exit is also automatic when the threat has passed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ads-b-receiver.rst:111
#: 5794cade2dd343798cb65f1e9847274f
msgid "To enable this feature connect with a Ground Station and set the following parameters:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ads-b-receiver.rst:113
#: bbb95b35ad534434b43315427d301324
msgid ":ref:`AVD_ENABLE <AVD_ENABLE>`: set to \"1\" to enable ADS-B based avoidance (param refresh may be necessary after setting this)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ads-b-receiver.rst:114
#: e01f3b08d7ee48038c930baefd551be1
msgid ":ref:`AVD_F_DIST_XY <AVD_F_DIST_XY>`: the horizontal distance in meters that should be considered a near-miss"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ads-b-receiver.rst:115
#: d64311b125be4f19849d4f9c4098d9ac
msgid ":ref:`AVD_F_DIST_Z <AVD_F_DIST_Z>`: the vertical distance in meters above or below the vehicle that should be considered a near-miss"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ads-b-receiver.rst:116
#: af59c3af56f24f05906be0cad7a616bc
msgid ":ref:`AVD_F_TIME <AVD_F_TIME>`: how many seconds in advance of a projected near-miss (based on the vehicle's current position and velocity) the vehicle should begin the ``AVD_F_ACTION``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ads-b-receiver.rst:117
#: 1ae1f0e66b85487885a6a026e24738d3
msgid ":ref:`AVD_F_ACTION <AVD_F_ACTION>`: controls how the vehicle should respond to a projected near-miss (i.e. 2:Climb Or Descend, 3:Move Horizontally, 4:Move Perpendicularly in 3D, 5:RTL or 6:Hover)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ads-b-receiver.rst:118
#: efa73b3d2f064b63bfd9b3e5252ccb83
msgid ":ref:`AVD_F_RCVRY <AVD_F_RCVRY>`: sets how the vehicle will behave after the vehicle has cleared the near-miss area (i.e. 1 = resume previous flight mode)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ads-b-receiver.rst:120
#: 9cf8c01b1a1b4b9986e5ab2cb92a0fdb
msgid "Note: there are equivalent \"Warn\" parameters (i.e. AVD_W_DIST_XY) that can be used to adjust when warnings to the pilot will appear on the ground station."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ads-b-receiver.rst:122
#: 54238b3bd9c4459fbdf1405aa471cbfe
msgid "In ArduPilot firmware versions 4.0 and later, the entry into this mode can be enabled or disabled via an RC channel switch by setting the channel's RCx_OPTION = 38 (ADSB Avoidance En). If the RC PWM is >1800us, then entry into this mode is enabled if a threat presents."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ads-b-receiver.rst:129
#: b51858c3753c43098390f5be5ae8f6a8
msgid "Vehicle Database"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ads-b-receiver.rst:131
#: d2e71943a6634584853064141b333bf4
msgid "When enabled, the ADS-B library will store information for up to 50 vehicles detected by the ADS-B receiver but can be further limited using the :ref:`ADSB_LIST_MAX<ADSB_LIST_MAX>` parameter. Due to some experimental work in other features, such as EKF2, available RAM may be limited. It is important to note that when ADS-B is disabled (:ref:`ADSB_TYPE<ADSB_TYPE>` = 0) then the memory is released, effectively freeing up about 1KB of RAM. When enabled, the detected vehicle list is checked once per second for potential conflicts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ads-b-receiver.rst:136
#: f2aeb7b6854a4feeb21eb1fcff59433c
msgid "Developer information including Simulation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ads-b-receiver.rst:137
#: 6a0713a30c0b438f84999d0d615f22ce
msgid "The data is transmitted via the `ADSB_VEHICLE message <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#ADSB_VEHICLE>`__. When received by ArduPilot, it is streamed out using the ``SRx_ADSB`` value where x is the telemetry port number and the value is how many vehicles per second to be streamed. If using telem1 the streamrate param would be ``SR1_ADSB``. The list will not repeat any faster than 1 second. This flexibility is useful to conserve bandwidth on data links but also allow maximum update rate for high-speed links such as an on-board companion computer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ads-b-receiver.rst:143
#: 79c61532d2b048b8b7acbaf9f65b1208
msgid "ArduPilot's SITL includes the simulation of ADS-B enabled aircraft. To enable this you must have pymavlink v1.1.70 or greater. If you have an older version, use:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ads-b-receiver.rst:151
#: 0099d98a0830488da1aa6c8da48031f3
msgid "Set the number of aircraft to simulate using the ``SIM_ADSB_COUNT`` parameter. Ping2020 simulation support can be enabled by setting parameter :ref:`SIM_ADSB_TX <SIM_ADSB_TX>`. Other simulation options for ADS-B are present, all starting with ``SIM_ADSB_``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ads-b-receiver.rst:155
#: 5bd633dac57d4d6fa1e267ef69d472ab
msgid "Plugging in a hardware ADS-B receiver to your computer using a USB-to-Serial converter, or using the PingUSB, will allow you to overlay real ADS-B traffic into the simulation.  You might invoke SITL in this way to achieve this effect:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ads-b-receiver.rst:162
#: f642490efb764dbf9a4ab2ab3845ac17
msgid "Where SERIAL_DEVICE might be /dev/serial/by-id/usb-FTDI_FT232R_USB_UART_A4008ZND-if00-port0 on a Linux system (find a list of valid serial devices with the command ``ls /dev/serial/by-id/*`` or ``ls /dev/ttyS*`` for a COM port on Cygwin).  Once SITL has started it may be necessary to set the ``SERIAL3_`` parameters:"
msgstr ""
